Q1: Rate limit kis basis par lagana hai?
------------------------------------------

Basis	                           Kab Use Karein
Per IP	                         Anonymous / unauthenticated endpoints ke liye
Per Identifier (Mobile/Email)	   Login/OTP endpoints pe — IP + Identifier combo best rehta hai
Per User (user_id / JWT sub)     Authenticated endpoints ke liye — jahan user ki authenticated identity available ho
Per API Key	                     Partner APIs / B2B integrations ke liye
Per Device ID	                   Mostly banking apps me — additional layer ke roop me


## Ideal Answer (interview me bolo):

Main Authenticated endpoints pe per-user, anonymous endpoints (login/OTP) pe per-IP + per-identifier combo, aur partner APIs pe per-API-key.



----------------------------------
Q2. Rate limit kahan baita hoga?
----------------------------------

Option A: API Gateway Level
- Gateway pe global rate limit per user enforce hoga — user ki total requests count karega across all services. 
  Jaise 10,000 req/min per user, chahe request kisi bhi service pe jaa rahi ho. Isse centralized view milta hai
  ki user overall kitna traffic generate kar raha hai.


Option B: Har Service Level
- Har service apna service-level per-user rate limit enforce karegi — regardless of its endpoints. 
  Jaise User Service: 5000 req/min per user, Payment Service: 100 req/min per user. 
  Matlab us service pe user ki total requests kitni allowed hain.


Option C: Hybrid (Recommended)
- Gateway pe global per-user limit + Service pe service-level user limit + Endpoint pe per-endpoint limit.
- Generally Hybrid use karte hain.


