Q3. Ek hi request pe multiple rate limits apply hongi?
---------------------------------------------------------

Example:

- Global: 10K/min per user (across all services)
- Service: 100/min per user (User Service), 200/min per user (Payment Service)
- Endpoint: 10/min per user (/payment/initiate)

Rule: Sabhi layers pass honi chahiye — ek bhi fail hui to request reject.


--------------------------------------------------
Q4. User tier ke basis pe different limits hongi?
--------------------------------------------------

Free: 100 req/min per free user
Premium: 1000 req/min per premium user 
Enterprise: unlimited per enterprise user

User tier user ki identity ka part hota hai. Is tier ke basis par alag-alag limits different layers pe enforce hoti hain:

- API Gateway level pe → Global tier-based limit apply hoti hai (across all services)
- Service level pe → Per-user, per-service tier-based limit
- Endpoint level pe → Per-user, per-service, per-endpoint tier-based limit

Tier JWT token claims se aata hai, agar hum JWT-based authentication use kar rahe hain.
- API Gateway pe: JWT verify karta hai → tier extract karta hai → global tier-based rate limit apply karta hai → phir tier ko header me daal ke service ko forward karta hai (jaise X-User-Tier: PREMIUM).
- Service pe: Header se tier read karti hai → apne rules ke according service-level aur endpoint-level tier-based rate limit apply karti hai.


