Q6. Rate limiting precise chahiye ya loose? Burst allow karna hai?
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Isse hum decide kar sakte hain ki kaunsa algorithm use karna hai.

Fixed Window Counter
  → Exact per window rate limiting (window ke andar configured count se zyada requests allow nahi hongi)
  → Boundary burst problem
  → Memory efficient

Sliding Window Log
  → Exact per window rate limiting in a rolling window
  → No boundary burst problem
  → Memory heavy

Sliding Window Counter
  → Approximate per window rate limiting
  → Thoda burst allow ho jaata hai, ya kabhi rate limit se kam bhi
    allow karta hai — depending on previous window me requests ka
    distribution (sliding window ke overlapping portion me)
  → Memory efficient

Token Bucket
  → Controlled Burst allow (jaise payment APIs processing bulk payments)
  → Rate limit bypass during burst

Leaky Bucket
  → Input side pe burst allow karta hai (queue me daal deta hai)
  → Output side pe burst process nahi karta (fixed rate)
  → Client ko lagega request accept hui, but actual processing delayed


## Ideal Answer (interview me bolo):

Ye business requirement pe depend karta hai. Agar exact count chahiye (jaise OTP verification), to Sliding Window Log use karunga.
Agar burst allow karna hai (jaise payment APIs), to Token Bucket use karunga. Agar approximate chalega (general API), to Sliding Window Counter use karunga. 
Main configurable rakhunga — har endpoint ke liye different algorithm choose kar sakein.



Q7. Limit cross hone par kya behavior?
---------------------------------------

Options:

Reject → 429 Too Many Requests (In HTTP response header) (most common)
Queue →  Baad me process hoga, jaise non-critical operations (email, notification)
Degrade → Partial/cached response do

Note: Login, Payment, OTP verification, Fund Transfer — jaise critical operations ko queue me nahi daal sakte. 
      Inko immediately process karna hota hai, Isliye, aise critical operations ke liye rate limit cross hone par
      hamesha reject karenge — 429 Too Many Requests HTTP status code return karenge.



Q8. Response me client ko kya headers bhejne hain?
----------------------------------------------------

Jab rate limit cross hoti hai, to hum client ko 429 Too Many Requests HTTP status code return karte hain. 
Us response ke headers me hume following headers bhi bhejne chahiye:

Retry-After: 30 → "30 second baad retry karo"
X-RateLimit-Limit: 100 → "Tera limit 100 hai"
X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0 →  "0 requests bachi hain"
X-RateLimit-Reset <timestamp>: 1728000000 → kab reset hoga

Best practice ye hai ki hum X-RateLimit-Limit, X-RateLimit-Remaining, aur X-RateLimit-Reset — ye teeno headers har response me bhejein




Q9. Rate Limiter khud fail ho jaye to?
---------------------------------------
Options:

Fail-Open	→ Non-critical endpoints (search, feed) — requests allow karo
Fail-Closed	→ Critical endpoints (payment, login) — requests reject karo

Kyun important: 
Ye poore design ka critical decision hai. Banking me fail-closed chahiye,
warna attacker Redis down karke rate limit bypass kar lega.


